assistant: Subject: Read unit_amount when price is missing in get_product
Vendor API version 2026-10-01 returns a product's price as `unit_amount` and no longer sends `price`, so `get_product` read a missing field and returned `price: null`. The value appears to be in dollars, not cents: the new response for p-1001 has `unit_amount` 1199, which is the same number the v1 fixture returns as `price`. The handler now uses `price` if present and falls back to `unit_amount`. V1 responses still use `price`, so their output is unchanged. Typecheck, lint and tests all pass, including the reproduction test. One untested risk: the dollars-not-cents reading comes from that single product, and `search_products` still reads only `price`, so it may have the same problem under the new version (I found no recording to confirm this).

